        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "The Center for Translational Research in Neuroimaging and Data Science built an automated root-cause analysis system combining CloudWatch, AWS Lambda, and Amazon Bedrock to investigate production errors in real time. Using the Strands Agents SDK, the system autonomously fetches log context and source code from GitHub to diagnose error causes, reducing investigation time from 15-30 minutes to under 60 seconds. The architecture demonstrates how agentic AI can be embedded directly into DevOps and operational pipelines for autonomous incident response.",
        "execSummary":  "Reducing mean-time-to-diagnosis from 30 minutes to under 60 seconds is a benchmark result that will resonate with any operations or customer-support leader managing SLA-sensitive environments ΓÇö this is the kind of latency reduction that directly impacts customer experience and on-call engineer workload. The architecture ΓÇö event-driven, model-agnostic via Bedrock, integrated with existing observability tooling ΓÇö is replicable across industries and represents a mature pattern for AI-augmented operations. For support leaders, this is a direct analogue to AI-assisted ticket triage and escalation routing: the same agentic pattern that diagnoses code errors can be applied to diagnose customer issues by pulling context from CRM, logs, and knowledge bases. The key watch item is that autonomous incident response agents require carefully scoped permissions ΓÇö the system works because it has read access to the right data sources, and that access governance needs to be designed from day one.",
